      "sources": [
        {
          "source_id": "eip",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "Hans Kobler is the Founder and Managing Partner of Energy Impact Partners (EIP), a $4.5+ billion global investment firm specialized to invest in the technologies powering the future of energy.",
          "quote_hash": "210778483ca367d67a4dcbb337234ad3575a95da006c3bdf49e0d6235292d510"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_launch",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "He launched EIP in 2015 on the premise of advancing climate innovation through collaboration.",
          "quote_hash": "42b83edde111520e2e1bb11d230196dc1bc88265874f67e7e74efd7d73025d15"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_hans",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "He started his career as a management consultant at Bain & Company before leading the energy technology group at GE Equity, General Electric’s venture capital arm. Hans went on to found and serve as CEO of Digital Power Capital, a venture capital fund focused on advanced power technologies. His entrepreneurial spirit then led him to build and lead ICx Technologies, a leading sensor technology company targeting security, transportation, and energy, which he took public on Nasdaq in 2007.",
          "quote_hash": "15c0052bf34ed2644ad52d9c77d49dc226788c6836b06cea1a1575d8bdd44f69"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_lindsay",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "Lindsay Luger is a Co-Founder of EIP, a global investment firm focused on energy transition technologies and our Sponsor, where she has served as Partner since October 2015. Ms. Luger has over a decade of experience investing in energy technology companies.",
          "quote_hash": "5bfee8d559ff487c4af5d47dd750dee916275fa98e07fbd37bbe7c6f0d030338"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_lindsay_career",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "Prior to joining EIP, Ms. Luger served as Vice President of Digital Power Capital from 2012 to 2015 and Vice President of Wexford Capital from 2007 to 2012.",
          "quote_hash": "ccc6d9ccc20845301211656dcb92c68c4fee0fe147c466d8b91c088d96c1eee7"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_sameer",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "While at EIP, he has led investments in Arcadia, Dragos, ERock (NYSE: EROC), ThinkLabs, Infravision, Urbint (acquired by Itron), Opus One (acquired by GE), Attivo (acquired by SentinelOne), Quilt, among others.",
          "quote_hash": "bbb8be052e1032a236c7441c3c7f59ea9e5294b95bc5b531882fd04649286947"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_sameer_career",
          "source_url": "https://www.energyimpactpartners.com/team/",
          "source_title": "team -",
          "source_content_hash": "08168cdea481e654fe304e8ba8dd6553d4300374128d883077559b794d128e90",
          "quote": "Prior to EIP, Sameer spent five years at Evercore in its Power and Renewable Energy Group where he advised clients on over $15 billion of M&A transactions. Prior to Evercore, he spent three years at GE Capital’s energy venture capital group focusing on industrial and clean tech investing.",
          "quote_hash": "b6b8a27a92400499ad100ded8f763b4c7b07cbb0db80c8f20e8def7fa24a584d"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "eip_contact",
